  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 251 PM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nBy Saturday, guidance is in good consensus with a gradual warming \ntrend as LREF temperature IQR spreads are around 5 degrees centered \non values in the upper 40s to low 50s, near seasonable normals. A \nshortwave trough slides southeastward into the area by Sunday \nresulting in leeside surface cyclogenesis and increasing \nprecipitation chances Sunday morning. Both the LREF and NBM have \nwidespread 90-100% chances for rain on Sunday with up to a 30% \nchance for >0.50\" for portions of the area. Current indications are \nthat rain should prevail with this system as surface temperatures \nare forecast to be in the 40s. However, it is worth noting that any \nsouthern shift with this trough and reflected surface feature would \nincrease chances across northern portions of the area for rain \nchanging to snow on the back end of things. This system brings a \ncold front through the area leading to cooler temperatures with \nhighs in the mid 40s to lower 50s on Monday. Another warming trend \nis expected by the middle of next week as probabilities for highs \n>50F get near 90-100% areawide by Wednesday.",
